       Float menu (WindowlessFloatMenuState). The selection announcement
       differentiates between a queued action (Shift held while clicking
       a colonist order) and a normal one. {0} = option label.
       The no-active-search focus announcement (label, disabled state,
       tooltip, position) now renders through AnnouncementComposer.ComposeFocus
       (element-uniformity campaign, task 8 packet B) instead of a hand-built
       key (see WindowlessFloatMenuState.ComposeOptionFocus). The keys below
       remain for the ExecuteSelected rejection message, the active-typeahead-
       search announcement (a shape the composer's fixed fragment order can't
       reproduce), and the search-tooltip variant.
       ================================================================= -->
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.FloatMenu.SelectedQueued>{0}, {1}</RimWorldAccess.UI.FloatMenu.SelectedQueued>
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.FloatMenu.Selected>{0} seleccionado</RimWorldAccess.UI.FloatMenu.Selected>
  <!-- Suffix appended to a disabled option label; active-search branch only
       (the no-search focus announcement speaks the standard disabled state
       word instead; see the composer retrofit note above). -->
  <!-- Spoken when activating a disabled float-menu option. {0} = option label. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.FloatMenu.LabelUnavailable>{0} - indisponível</RimWorldAccess.UI.FloatMenu.LabelUnavailable>
  <!-- Tooltip variant inside an active typeahead search; the search
       buffer suffix is appended by typeahead.BuildSearchContextSuffix(),
       so this key does not include the query. -->

